From 769c1126266920950d3e06985372fd272d23be0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 12:07:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Restore the Super Booster Rocket Boots ride (I-340)

Quest 24942 "Zombies vs. Super Booster Rocket Boots": item 84320 played no
animation, summoned nothing and banked exactly one kill credit per click.

The port had wired 72891 to the generic spell_zep_fixed_credit<38807> template,
which credits the caster on ANY effect hit without looking at what was hit. The
spell self-casts, so every click paid a free credit. It was standing in for the
whole mechanic, because none of the four spells behind it had been ported.

- spell_zep_q24942_zombies_booster is now the real donor handler
  (SpellEffects.cpp:4446): quest active + not already riding -> cast 72889. It
  grants no credit; Goblin Zombie 38753 carries KillCredit1 = 38807, so the fire
  nova killing it pays the objective once per zombie.
- spell_zep_fixed_credit<Entry> deleted. After I-281, I-318 and this it had no
  users left and every use it ever had was a bug.
- New AuraScript spell_zep_q24942_boots_ride on 72887 lights the burning aura
  72885 on the rider. It cannot live on the boots' CreatureAI: a CAN_CONTROL
  seat charms the vehicle (Vehicle.cpp:432) and CreatureAI::OnCharmed sets
  IsAIEnabled = false (CreatureAI.cpp:54), which gates out both PassengerBoarded
  (Vehicle.cpp:496) and UpdateAI for the whole ride. 72887's DUMMY effect on the
  rider is co-terminous with the ride and AC removes it itself on exit, so apply
  and remove are guaranteed there. Retail did the same job with 72897 "AICast on
  Enter Seat" (effect 160, TARGET_UNIT_MASTER), which 3.3.5a has no equivalent
  for.

Closes I-340

